        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(security): add ReDoS guard to exec approval argPattern matching",
        "body": "Fixes #90014\n\n## Problem\n\n`matchArgPattern` in `src/infra/exec-command-resolution.ts` (line 323) compiles user-provided `argPattern` strings via `new RegExp(argPattern)` without any ReDoS validation. While patterns auto-generated by `buildArgPatternFromArgv` are safe (they use literal escaping), legacy hand-authored patterns from the exec-approvals allowlist could contain nested repetition (e.g., `(a+)+$`) that causes catastrophic backtracking.\n\n## Fix\n\nSafety-check with `compileSafeRegexDetailed`, then compile the original `argPattern` with `new RegExp(argPattern)`. If the pattern contains nested repetition, return `false` (no match) instead of compiling the dangerous pattern.\n\n**Key design choice:** The guard calls `hasNestedRepetition` (validation only) then compiles with `new RegExp(argPattern)` using the **original untrimmed pattern text**. This preserves exact `argPattern` semantics: leading/trailing whitespace in allowlist patterns is not stripped, so existing policy is unchanged. An earlier revision used `compileSafeRegex` which trims `.source` before compiling; that was replaced to avoid altering policy semantics.\n\nThe production diff is +4 lines (1 import, 3 guard lines). No CHANGELOG changes.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nBehavior addressed: ReDoS-vulnerable argPattern entries in exec-approval allowlists could hang via nested repetition. Safety validation rejects them, then the original untrimmed argPattern is compiled so legacy whitespace-sensitive policies are unchanged.\n\nReal environment tested: macOS darwin arm64, worktree /tmp/oc-proof-82950 on branch fix/exec-approval-redos-guard rebased onto upstream/main, Node via node --import tsx and vitest.\n\nExact steps or command run after this patch:\n```bash\ncd /tmp/oc-proof-82950\nCI=true pnpm install --frozen-lockfile\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs run src/infra/exec-command-resolution.test.ts\nnode --import tsx scripts/proof-exec-argpattern-redos.mjs\n```\n\nEvidence after fix: terminal output copied below.\n\n```console\n1) ReDoS reject\n  matchAllowlist => null\n  warn => [\n  '[exec-approvals] Rejected argPattern with unsafe nested repetition'\n]\n2) Safe pattern match\n  matchAllowlist(script.py) => ^script\\.py$\n3) Whitespace semantics (original text, not trimmed compile)\n  argv script.py => null\n  argv ' script.py ' =>  script\\.py \n  trimmed-compile would match bare script.py => true\nRESULT: PASS\n```\n\nObserved result after fix: Unsafe nested-repetition patterns return no allowlist match and emit the exec-approvals warn; safe ^script.py$ matches; patterns with leading/trailing spaces keep original semantics (bare script.py does not match \" script.py \", while the spaced argv does). compileSafeRegexDetailed would have matched the bare string after trim.\n\nWhat was not tested: Live gateway exec approval prompt against a production allowlist file with a real user shell session.\n\n",
